# First Roll: the first of our levels, twice the length of the original's first and harder, in its spirit (its order of
# lessons, its kinds of parts, its help; measured, not traced: the layout, turns, heights and lengths are ours). Four
# long sectors that teach the wooden ball, the paper one and the stone one and then use them:
#  1. (wood, paper, wood) off the tower over a wooden bridge, the first rails, boxes on a walled square, a wavy road,
#     curving rails, crates shoved off a bare stretch, the stone transformer and a loose stone ball, the wood one
#     hidden beside a climb the stone ball cannot make, loose paper balls, the paper transformer and three fans up to
#     the floors above, a plate bridge, back to wood, rails;
#  2. (wood, stone) a loop of rails, a wooden bridge, a seesaw, a terrace of short turns, a second loop, turning arms,
#     a dome, long rails, the stone on the crate (rammed out from under it from the floor below, the stone
#     transformer there), stacked boxes, crates shoved off a bare stretch, humps, loose balls, long rails;
#  3. (stone) a square of loose balls, humps, rails, two pairs of pushers pushed from the floors beside their lanes,
#     crates shoved off, a bare terrace, a second stone on its crate, a long rail descent, the wood transformer;
#  4. (wood) a wavy way, wooden ramps up between railed landings, a seesaw, a plate bridge, swinging sacks over a
#     railed stretch, a terrace, rails, rails spiralling down, loose balls on the long way down, the finish.
# Gutters along most floors; railings at the start, round the outer side of the turns, on the landings and where a
# floor below the way has a drop; bare stretches and long rails grow towards the end.
# Edit this file and run `scripts/own-levels.sh assets/levels/01_First_Roll`.
